    "bio": "a Representative from California; born in Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, Calif., October 12, 1951; graduated from Katella High School, Anaheim, Calif., 1970; B.A., California State University, Fullerton, Calif., 1977; business owner; corporate tax manager; member of the California state senate, 1983-1993; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Third and to the twelve succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1993-January 3, 2019); chair, Committee on Foreign Affairs (One Hundred Thirteenth through One Hundred Fifteenth Congresses); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Sixteenth Congress in 2018.",
